  "layoutMapUrl": null,
  "signatureHoleDescription": "Hole 18 is the only par 5 at Perkerson — 485 feet of woodsy finish that rewards three clean shots. It's the hole that defines the course's championship character: no gifts, no shortcuts, just honest disc golf through the trees to close the round. Par here feels like a small victory.",
  "localTips": "This is Atlanta's hardest free course — bring your accuracy and your patience. The par 5 on 18 is your one chance to make up ground. Rubber tees can get slick after rain; wear good shoes. Free to play near downtown.",
